{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RootsOfUnityProduct","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RootsOfUnityProduct","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.RootsOfUnity.PrimitiveRoots","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.Cyclotomic.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Circle"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.prod_two_sin_pi_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.prod_two_sin_pi_div","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RootsOfUnityProduct.lean#L101-L155","doc":"**`∏_{j=1}^{n-1} 2 sin(jπ/n) = n`.**\n\nThe real form, obtained from `prod_one_sub_zeta_pow` at `ζ = e^{2πi/n}` by\ntaking norms, using `‖1 - e^{iθ}‖ = 2 sin(θ/2)` on `(0, 2π)`.\n\nAt `k = n-1` this is `s_{n-1} = -log n` for\n`s_k = -∑_{j=1}^k log(2 sin(jπ/n))`, the endpoint that pins the additive\nconstant in the one-loop expansion of `QOU.Knot.kashaev`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.prod_one_sub_zeta_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.prod_one_sub_zeta_pow","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RootsOfUnityProduct.lean#L75-L99","doc":"**`∏_{j=1}^{n-1}(1 - ζ^j) = n`** for a primitive `n`-th root of unity `ζ`.\n\nThe index conversion needs no injectivity: `Multiset.map_erase_of_mem` holds for\nany `f`, because multiset `erase` removes a single occurrence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.prod_one_sub_nthRoots_erase_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.prod_one_sub_nthRoots_erase_one","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RootsOfUnityProduct.lean#L46-L73","doc":"**`∏_{ζ ≠ 1}(1 - ζ) = n`** over the `n`-th roots of unity in `ℂ`.\n\nThe product is over `(nthRoots n 1).erase 1`, i.e. every `n`-th root of unity\nexcept `1` itself, each counted once (the roots are distinct since `n ≠ 0` in\n`ℂ`, which is what `card_nthRoots_one` encodes). ","signatureChunk":0}]}